{
 "id": "example",
 "name": "flight-scrubber",
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Scrub through a flight on a map",
 "summary": "MAP-03's flight tracker with a Slider bound to the progress: dragging it moves the plane along the great-circle route, extends the flown part and counts the time left down (an 8-hour flight, so the app only sends the progress). The route points and the time left read the slider's live value because the expander declares them after the slider.",
 "prompt": "A flight tracker card: New York to London on a map, the plane along the route at the flight's progress, the time left, and a slider to scrub through the flight.",
 "level": 3,
 "family": "HOME",
 "capabilities": {
  "primary": [
   "map.marker",
   "map.region",
   "map.route",
   "input.drag"
  ],
  "secondary": [
   "draw.path",
   "host.variables",
   "text.dynamic",
   "data.expression"
  ]
 },
 "use_cases": [
  "map",
  "travel",
  "card"
 ],
 "form_factor": "phone",
 "keywords": [
  "delivery tracker map",
  "flight map",
  "flight path",
  "flight scrubber",
  "flight tracker",
  "great circle",
  "path between cities",
  "plane",
  "plane heading",
  "progress on a map",
  "route",
  "route on a map",
  "scrub progress",
  "slider on a map",
  "tracker map"
 ],
 "teaches": [
  "A Slider bound to an exported variable (\"value\": \"@progress\") presets it from the app and drives everything that reads it after the slider; resources variables that read it (the route point, the time left) are moved after the slider by the expander, so put the slider ABOVE the map in the tree",
  "Derive what you can from one input: the time left is 480 * (1 - @progress), so the slider moves the plane and the clock together"
 ],
 "inputs": {
  "variables": {
   "progress": {
    "type": "float",
    "meaning": "Flight progress 0..1",
    "default": 0.42,
    "min": 0,
    "max": 1,
    "step": 0.01
   }
  },
  "clock": null,
  "touch": true
 },
